Datasheet‑style version (concise)
1. Overview
Name: AHD‑TV‑1 Single‑Dot Illusion Engine

Type: Analog timing + envelope system with optional MCU control

Output: Single bright dot (CRT or LED) with HD/UHD‑class temporal illusion

2. Modes
Frame rates:

MODE_NTSC_30 → ~29.97 fps

MODE_AHD_100 → 100 fps

MODE_AHD_1000 → ~1000 fps

Illusion classes (virtual resolution):

L0 → LDTV (~400×300)

L1 → SD 480

L2 → HD 720

L3 → Full HD 1080

L4 → 4K

L5 → 8K

L6 → 16K / 24k‑line‑class

3. Profiles
Breathing Field: smooth luma sinusoid

Chromatic Drift: color phase cycling

Ghostwave: blink‑synced scene cuts

Whiteout: full‑field flash

Static Field: constant brightness

4. Hardware blocks
Master oscillator: 3.579545 MHz crystal (NTSC burst)

Divider chain: transistor flip‑flops → frame, field, phase clocks

Selectors: transistor networks for:

frame‑rate tap (mode)

pulse‑width/phase network (class)

envelope RC network (profile)

Dot driver: NPN transistor driving CRT video input or LED

5. MCU hook
Input: field sync pulse (~60 Hz or chosen rate)

Outputs (7 pins):

MODE_SEL[1:0]

CLASS_SEL[2:0]

PROFILE_SEL[1:0]

Function:

Flip mode/class/profile only at field boundaries

Does not generate timing; only selects analog networks

6. Use cases
CRT center‑spot illusion box

LED‑dot “HD illusion” display

Hybrid analog/digital experiment with MCU‑driven presets
